From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] zram-on: do not loop for ever on a kernel without "managed" in zoneinfo

zram-on.sh sizes the zram disk from the Normal and HighMem zones in /proc/zoneinfo. It waited,
with `until ... = "managed"`, for the zone's "managed" line, which Linux 3.4 does not print: the
loop read to the end of the file and kept going on the last line, at 11% of a core, so the disk
size was never written, swap-on.sh failed with "read swap header failed" and the device ran
without swap (seen on the Galaxy Tab Pro 10.1, which has 1.7 GB of RAM and 48 MB free with the
UI up).

Read the two lines with awk instead: "managed" where the kernel prints it, as before, and
"present" where it does not. On the tablet that is 518157 pages, a 506 MB zram disk.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/common/lib/systemd/system/scripts/zram-on.sh.in	2026-10-05 09:24:57.726306902 +0200
+++ b/common/lib/systemd/system/scripts/zram-on.sh.in	2026-10-05 09:24:57.749721330 +0200
@@ -72,20 +72,13 @@
         fi
 
         # get total free
-        TOTAL_FREE=0
-        while read line
-        do
-            ZONE=`echo $line | awk '/^Node/ {print $4}'`
-            if [ "$ZONE" = "Normal" ] || [ "$ZONE" = "HighMem" ]
-            then
-                read line
-                until [ "`echo $line | awk '{print $1}'`" = "managed" ]; do
-                    read line
-                done
-                ZONESIZE=`echo $line | awk '{print $2}'`
-                TOTAL_FREE=`expr $TOTAL_FREE + $ZONESIZE`
-            fi
-        done < /proc/zoneinfo
+        # Pages in the Normal and HighMem zones: "managed" where the kernel prints it, "present" where it
+        # does not. The loop that stood here waited for a "managed" line and never ended on a 3.4 kernel,
+        # which prints none: zram-on.sh spun for ever, the disk size was never set and swap never came on.
+        TOTAL_FREE=`awk '/^Node/ { zone = $4; next }
+                         (zone == "Normal" || zone == "HighMem") && $1 == "present" { present[zone] = $2 }
+                         (zone == "Normal" || zone == "HighMem") && $1 == "managed" { managed[zone] = $2 }
+                         END { for (z in present) total += (z in managed) ? managed[z] : present[z]; print total + 0 }' /proc/zoneinfo`
         TOTAL_FREE=$(($TOTAL_FREE*$PAGE_SIZE/1024/1024))
 
         if [ $TOTAL_FREE -lt $BASE_FREE ]; then
